From 94c0ff48276c5017313ef81f53681b58103281b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chao Liu <chao.liu@processmission.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 19:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci: accept completion at timeout boundary

The interrupt status can acquire all requested completion bits during the
last status read at the timeout boundary.  Do not report -ETIMEDOUT when that
read already proves the command completed.

This matters for emulated controllers where a command-register write can
perform enough synchronous DMA work for the command timer to cross its
deadline before software reads the already-set completion bit.

Signed-off-by: Chao Liu <chao.liu@processmission.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/sdhci.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
index ad9d7dfa03..cb3cdc8592 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
@@ -303,7 +303,8 @@ static int sdhci_send_command(struct mmc *mmc, struct mmc_cmd *cmd,
 		if (stat & SDHCI_INT_ERROR)
 			break;
 
-		if (get_timer(start) >= SDHCI_READ_STATUS_TIMEOUT) {
+		if ((stat & mask) != mask &&
+		    get_timer(start) >= SDHCI_READ_STATUS_TIMEOUT) {
 			if (host->quirks & SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_R1B) {
 				return 0;
 			} else {
-- 
